1
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:26,840
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:34,020
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:42,180
Chalking the head of the PE teacher,

4
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:48,440
they laughed at me for
still acting like a kid.

5
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if you bring out your spirit,
Katsushika is always the same.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,520
The yawn-inducing streets that
never change are strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:10,460
From the pointed-roofed water pavilion,

8
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls into the vast sky.

9
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it?

10
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,040
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

11
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,760
Only after losing it did I realize.

12
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,840
Because I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,360
This is the person I like.

14
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,280
Yes, yes, yes.

15
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:51,180
Wow, that's nice!

16
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:56,020
The eyes that had only been looking at
the lifeless high-rise buildings of the city

17
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,900
seem to be slowly opening
up to something beautiful.

18
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:00,980
Look at how many dragonflies there are!

19
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:04,480
In Komachi-chan's countryside,

20
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:07,240
they say there are not only
dragonflies but lots of fireflies too.

21
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,940
Really? I can't wait!

22
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:13,540
Ke-chan,
you seem to have turned back into a child.

23
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:14,920
Hey, Komachi-chan.

24
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,640
Yeah, right?

25
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,600
Good thing we kept it from Ryo-chan

26
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:27,160
Even in a place overflowing with nature like this,
luxuriously,

27
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:30,640
there's bound to be noise about games and karaoke,
you know.

28
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:34,640
R-Reiko-san, speak of the devil! Behind you!

29
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,300
Huh?

30
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,400
Can I help you with something?

31
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:44,000
No, it's nothing, really. Sorry.

32
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,700
Well? Did I scare you?

33
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:49,280
Ke-chan, you're impossible.

34
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:53,160
I was just trying to scare you a little.

35
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:54,500
We have to do something about this.

36
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:56,960
The house keeps getting closer and closer.

37
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:02,860
Hey, Mom, what's the meaning of this?

38
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:06,780
So, Komachi, did you like any of them?

39
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:10,840
Like them?
I don't even want to get married yet!

40
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,260
You're coming home for summer break anyway,

41
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:15,580
so why not go on a marriage
meeting while you're at it?

42
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:16,880
No way.

43
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:21,840
Don't let my looks fool you.
I've got a boyfriend or two, you know.

44
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,560
That's obviously a lie.

45
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,380
It's not a lie!

46
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:27,300
I really do have a boyfriend!

47
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,360
Then bring that person home to meet us.

48
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:30,920
What?

49
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:33,160
If you can't bring them,

50
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:36,680
I'm going to arrange a meeting on my own.

51
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:37,440
What?

52
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:39,980
Fine, I get it.

53
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,460
I'll bring them along to
see you over summer break.

54
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:47,680
Don't you dare. I absolutely
don't want any arranged meetings.

55
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:53,920
But what do I do?
I need to find a boyfriend quickly.

56
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:07,020
Mr. Nakagawa is the only one I can use as my boyfriend.
It doesn't have to be a real relationship.

57
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:12,380
If only he'd agree to play my boyfriend,
at least while we're in the countryside.

58
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,620
I'm going to go buy some bento.

59
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:22,880
Just me and Nakagawa.

60
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,380
Now's the time to ask.

61
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:28,120
Um, Nakagawa...

62
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,640
Well, look who's here.
So you two were hiding out here.

63
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:32,020
W-what the...

64
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:34,320
S-senpai, how did you get here?

65
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:38,400
What, you think I'd walk? I had a Honda
bike take me to the station the other day.

66
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,158
I'd heard it was the countryside,

67
00:04:41,208 --> 00:04:43,140
three and a half hours
on the express from Tokyo,

68
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:46,860
then six hours one way
with trains and buses.

69
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:49,620
In six hours you could go abroad!

70
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:56,540
What are you doing here, Kankichi?

71
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,720
You're not leaving me out,
no matter how hard you try.

72
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:03,140
Reiko, you did buy my share too, right?

73
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,600
Ke-chan, so you followed us after all.

74
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:17,480
I'm not joking!
You really plan on tagging along?

75
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,442
Of course,

76
00:05:18,492 --> 00:05:21,740
you never know what kind of trouble
young people might get into on their own.

77
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:23,880
I won't make any mistakes.

78
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:24,779
That's right,

79
00:05:24,829 --> 00:05:29,200
your tagging along is the biggest blunder of all,
a total disaster!

80
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,420
This guy isn't even a true Edokko,
so don't talk like one!

81
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,340
Coming from a gorilla raised in the jungle!

82
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:39,060
What about you,
lying about your age on your day off?

83
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:40,700
Don't go around dressed
like a high school girl!

84
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:44,720
You're one to talk!
At least dress decently on your day off.

85
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,740
That's right, come at me!

86
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:48,660
Your nose hairs are sticking out!

87
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,860
I absolutely won't take you along!

88
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:54,160
I'm definitely coming along.

89
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:56,280
Now, now, senpai.

90
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:59,180
You've followed us this far,
so there's no helping it.

91
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:03,740
I'd rather die than be
stuck with a man like this.

92
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:07,060
I'll stick to you like a cockroach,
no matter where you go.

93
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:11,060
We will arrive at the Oyama River shortly.

94
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,280
We have to get off at the next stop.

95
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:15,740
The next one?

96
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,100
We got off.

97
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:28,760
We have to transfer to
another train from here, right?

98
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,940
Which way do we go?

99
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:39,260
Wasn't it...?

100
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:40,820
Actually, it's next autumn.

101
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:44,060
I already told you we're
not taking you along!

102
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:48,220
So you tricked me, Komachi!

103
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:50,820
I'm not one to give up
over something like this!

104
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:54,300
Alright!

105
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:55,720
Go!

106
00:06:55,720 --> 00:07:22,380
Nooooooooo... no!

107
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:23,900
That feels refreshing.

108
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:28,040
Having that caveman tagging
along ruined the mood!

109
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:32,620
But I don't think Senpai
would give up that easily.

110
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,120
Yeah, you're right.

111
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:38,040
I'm going to make a quick phone call.

112
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:43,480
This is my chance.
If I'm going to confess, it has to be now.

113
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:48,180
Um, Nakagawa-san...

114
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:50,580
Th-that...

115
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,200
We caught up! They're ours now!

116
00:07:55,580 --> 00:08:00,140
Ugh! That was my chance!
You idiot, Ryo-chan!

117
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,000
Hey! I'm coming along on the trip, Nakagawa!

118
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,020
Hyah!

119
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,020
What?

120
00:08:11,540 --> 00:08:12,880
Then please do it that way.

121
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:17,340
Wasn't that Ryo-chan just now...?

122
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:19,420
I wonder if I'm just imagining things.

123
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:37,420
Damn, we missed it by a hair.

124
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:38,960
When's the next bus?

125
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:42,380
What?! There's only one bus a day?

126
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,720
Thanks for your hard work.

127
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:50,580
Next stop, the last one:
Oinaga Village Elementary School.

128
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:52,940
Oinaga Village Elementary School.

129
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:55,760
Even Ryo-chan can't follow us all the way out here,
it seems.

130
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:57,360
You never know.

131
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,260
When it comes to the senpai's persistence,

132
00:08:59,260 --> 00:09:01,380
he's truly more persistent than a cockroach.

133
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:05,340
We got here and I still couldn't tell him.

134
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,500
Go, go, run!

135
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,280
This one!

136
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,880
No, not that! Hurry!

137
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,180
I'm home.

138
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:37,540
You must be exhausted from such a long trip.

139
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,620
Thank you for having us.

140
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:44,720
Mom, Dad, this is Reiko-senpai, and this is

141
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,460
our great senior, Ryotsu.

142
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:50,440
Wow, there really is nothing here, is there?

143
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,300
Ryo-chan.

144
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:53,580
So you caught up after all?

145
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:54,680
Of course.

146
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:58,220
Mom, it's a blessing there's
chilled watermelon, but

147
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,140
Mom.

148
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,120
It's fine, Mom.

149
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,980
Just let him sleep in the cowshed.

150
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,280
It's a cowshed, you know!

151
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:12,320
Ha ha even the cow says so!

152
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:15,100
Shut up!
Can you understand what cows are saying?

153
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:17,240
Just as expected of a country bumpkin.

154
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,660
You said that I'll take care of you, shorty.

155
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,660
This spirited girl...

156
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:26,480
These two are always like this.
They're perfectly in sync, right?

157
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:29,200
I guess they say the more you fight,
the closer you are.

158
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,420
I'm Nakagawa.

159
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:37,307
Konyakonyakonya! You damn... you bastard!

160
00:10:37,357 --> 00:10:38,915
Let go, it hurts!

161
00:10:38,965 --> 00:10:41,700
Ow ow you bastard!

162
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:45,175
Well, well, please come on in.

163
00:10:45,225 --> 00:10:48,600
The watermelon's chilled,
and we have fresh-picked tomatoes too.

164
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,940
Watermelon?

165
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,120
Thank you for the food, Mom.

166
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:55,600
Hey, Ke-chan! Don't come in covered in mud!

167
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,240
It's really relaxing here, isn't it.

168
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,500
I'm glad we came.

169
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:24,980
It really is.

170
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,340
He's so manly,

171
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:33,300
he's actually a pretty good guy, isn't he?

172
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:34,500
Yeah.

173
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,600
We don't have time to relax.

174
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:42,480
I need to ask Nakagawa to
be my fake boyfriend soon.

175
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,520
Can't we somehow get some time alone?

176
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:50,620
The corn's boiled. Would you like one?

177
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,240
Thank you.

178
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:57,700
Ryo-chan really has no sense of restraint,
does he?

179
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:01,420
It's better that way,
having someone so easygoing.

180
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:05,020
Since we may be getting along
for a long time from now on.

181
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,700
That's so true.

182
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:19,480
There's a river flowing nearby

183
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:23,420
Let's go check out the river, shall we?

184
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:25,200
Sounds good, let's go.

185
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,720
There it is! Did it go that way?

186
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:32,400
There!

187
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,600
It got away!

188
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:34,640
Here!

189
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,980
It went that way!

190
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:38,640
Over there! Over there!

191
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:39,400
What should we do?

192
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:40,460
We've got to catch it, no matter what!

193
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,620
What do we do?

194
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,700
There's one over there!

195
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,120
Chance! Chance!

196
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:48,580
Alright, leave it to me!

197
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,700
Please, big brother!

198
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:51,740
There!

199
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:53,380
How about that? I did it!

200
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,480
Ahahahaha

201
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,660
Not fair -

202
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,360
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

203
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,040
Getting toyed with by a fish, are you?

204
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:04,920
You'll never catch a thief like that.

205
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:07,500
Ahahaha

206
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,540
Don't worry, I'll handle it from here.

207
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:10,540
Eeh?

208
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,220
Who?

209
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,580
Eeh?

210
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:13,860
Yay!

211
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,340
Who, who, who?

212
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:18,240
A sandal!

213
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,200
Who's that?

214
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,480
Nakagawa, don't lose!

215
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,540
Go!

216
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:23,500
Eeh?

217
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,260
Ahahaha

218
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,540
This guy really is in the way, isn't he?

219
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:44,400
What, you're still
treating me like a nuisance?

220
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,268
But it's the truth,

221
00:13:46,318 --> 00:13:48,760
I said you're in the way
because you are in the way.

222
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:51,660
Don't you dare wear a hat like that,
you tomboy.

223
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,820
It's a big act.

224
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,400
That's actually not bad at all.

225
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:06,860
Isn't there some way I
can get Nakagawa alone?

226
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:10,160
That was fun.

227
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:12,740
Countryside's really nice, isn't it?

228
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:16,120
Hey, hey, I just thought of something.

229
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:18,340
Why don't we pair up
and do a test of courage?

230
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:20,680
There's a perfect spot nearby.

231
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:22,280
A test of courage.

232
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:39,740
So this is where we're
doing the courage test.

233
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,860
This tunnel is really old.

234
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:45,080
Yeah, it looks like the line
was abandoned decades ago.

235
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:48,720
People say a ghost train
runs through this tunnel.

236
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:50,400
A ghost train?

237
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,380
Really?

238
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:52,920
Really, for real.

239
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:56,500
It's from the time of the Pacific War,
you know.

240
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,120
There was an air raid,

241
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:05,760
and the bombing caved in the tunnel,

242
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:13,540
and a train got crushed beneath it.
Everyone on board apparently died.

243
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:18,460
After that came the defeat,
and only the rails were left.

244
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,740
Exactly at midnight,
when the bombing happened,

245
00:15:28,660 --> 00:15:30,520
They say that train comes running through.

246
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:33,820
carrying passengers who
turned into skeletons.

247
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:38,220
The inner part should still be
sealed off just as it was back then.

248
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:42,060
Then it's Reiko and the caveman as a pair.

249
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:43,640
I'll pair with Nakagawa.

250
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:47,120
Let's make it a race to see who can
get to the end and come back first.

251
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,680
Sounds fun, doesn't it?

252
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:49,960
Let's go, Nakagawa.

253
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:56,380
Hey, hey,
you're seriously going to do a courage test?

254
00:15:57,860 --> 00:16:01,500
This way,
I can be alone with Ke-chan, right?

255
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:03,840
And what are you going to do
once you're alone with him?

256
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:07,160
I've been thinking Komachi-chan
has been acting strange lately.

257
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:08,760
What are you talking about?

258
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:11,740
It's none of your business, Ryo-chan.

259
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:24,140
We're finally alone,
but I can't get the words out.

260
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:25,840
I have to say it soon.

261
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,280
Nakagawa...

262
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:36,180
I have a rather presumptuous favor to ask.

263
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:39,560
It's like I'm confessing.

264
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,340
A favor?

265
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:48,020
Nakagawa, you're bold.

266
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:51,180
Go on, give it a try.

267
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:57,820
It only needs to be the person here with me,
that's all.

268
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,620
In front of Dad and Mom,

269
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,240
my

270
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:03,920
love

271
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:07,340
could you pretend to be my boyfriend?

272
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:14,560
What is it?

273
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,920
That's an easy favor to grant.

274
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,700
Are you really sure?

275
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:21,660
Of course.

276
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:27,000
I've been your lover
since the day I was born.

277
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:30,620
I'll never let you go, not for all eternity.

278
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:32,720
Nakagawa-san.

279
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,320
I'm so happy! I'm going to be happy!

280
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:40,040
Now, a kiss of love...

281
00:17:45,740 --> 00:18:10,300
N-no! !

282
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,920
No, nice to meet you.

283
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:15,140
Then, whose voice was that just now?
Nakagawa's?

284
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,840
Take that one step further.

285
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:18,476
Come on,

286
00:18:18,526 --> 00:18:22,594
let's share a kiss of love,
just the two of us.

287
00:18:22,644 --> 00:18:23,560
Japan

288
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:26,120
This is the worst.

289
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:31,500
Who on earth put a revolving
door out in a place like this?

290
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:33,800
I'm not being pushy, you know.

291
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,900
Mr. Nakagawa,

292
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:41,560
I'm sorry! It's not like that!

293
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,000
A kiss of love?

294
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:48,360
Why?

295
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:50,000
I did it again.

296
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:57,240
What is going on, anyway?

297
00:18:57,240 --> 00:19:00,380
And I thought we'd finally pulled it off.

298
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:02,200
It's that old geezer Gorbo!

299
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:04,360
What are you doing out here?

300
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:07,300
It's ninja camp training.

301
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:09,400
We're going to get caught.

302
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,500
Farewell!

303
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:12,400
What are you doing?!

304
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:14,340
Ahahaha!

305
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:19,720
You're hiding too slowly!

306
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:22,200
Don't look, you pervert!

307
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:29,660
So Gorbo's inside this tunnel too

308
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,780
Knowing how seriously scared
he is of this kind of thing.

309
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,860
If he finds out there's a
ghost train in this tunnel...

310
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,980
Oh no, it's Gorbo!

311
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:46,140
I ate sand!

312
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,100
Gorbo!

313
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,720
Idiot!

314
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:54,840
It's me, it's me!

315
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:58,280
Ryotsu, why are you in a place like this?

316
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,140
So that's what it is.

317
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,640
B-but is it really true?

318
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:09,420
Th-this tunnel has gh...

319
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:11,900
A ghost train

320
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:25,560
If there were such a thing,
the tunnel would have collapsed by now.

321
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,720
Gramps.

322
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,480
Speaking of which, what time is it now?

323
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:32,120
Uh -

324
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:35,860
It's exactly midnight.

325
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:39,240
Ugh, suddenly I've gotten really scared.

326
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:41,760
Hey, let's go back.

327
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:42,940
Yeah, let's.

328
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:44,780
What are you scared of?

329
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:47,460
You're the one who suggested the courage test,
remember?

330
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,880
Well, that's easy for you to say.

331
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:53,420
A ghost train is just a made-up story,
so don't let it get to you...

332
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,820
The tracks are vibrating!

333
00:20:58,820 --> 00:20:59,460
Not again.

334
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:02,620
And don't even try to scare us again!

335
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:05,760
It's not a lie, put your foot on it.

336
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,180
It's real.

337
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:11,340
But the line's been abandoned,
so how can this be?

338
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:14,080
Something's coming along the rails.

339
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,280
What do you mean, something?

340
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,280
How should I know?

341
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:26,980
It's coming!

342
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:36,420
It's the real ghost train!

343
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,340
No way.

344
00:21:39,860 --> 00:21:42,600
Leave the rest to us, I say.

345
00:21:48,380 --> 00:22:07,580
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

346
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:20,460
This one's not it!

347
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:22,200
It's a diesel locomotive.

348
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:24,220
Watch out!

349
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:26,900
What are you two doing in a place like this?

350
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,920
What are you doing here, old man?

351
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,680
We're growing mushrooms.

352
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:31,440
Mushrooms?

353
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:35,820
The inside of the tunnel is damp,
so it's perfect for growing mushrooms.

354
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,740
We harvest them at night.

355
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:42,500
Hey, don't go causing confusion like that.

356
00:22:44,700 --> 00:22:45,920
What's that sound?

357
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:51,300
That was a missile just now!

358
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:53,380
Damn! It was auto-tracking!

359
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,340
What an idiot!

360
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:05,440
What's that noise?

361
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:15,600
You two aren't seriously going that far,
are you?

362
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:19,720
What are you talking about, Dad?

363
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:23,440
Ryotsu, my daughter is an unworthy girl,

364
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:26,160
but please take good care
of her for years to come.

365
00:23:28,380 --> 00:23:30,740
That's a huge misunderstanding!

366
00:23:30,740 --> 00:23:33,340
Me, give this headstrong girl to you?

367
00:23:33,900 --> 00:23:35,020
No way!

368
00:23:35,020 --> 00:23:38,580
Same here, no way!
Seriously, I'm so pissed off.

369
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:39,620
What?

370
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,440
What on earth happened?

371
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:44,080
Yeah.

372
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:46,360
There must be all sorts of reasons.

373
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:50,500
Anyway, it doesn't seem to concern us,
does it, mushroom man?

374
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:56,720
I hate you!

375
00:24:05,020 --> 00:24:07,160
I thought it was some
tough prehistoric warrior...

376
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,220
So it was a meteorite from space?

377
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:11,400
And then I thought, my body became light.

378
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:14,300
And then I thought, now it's getting heavy!

379
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:16,720
It's you again, Professor Esaki!

380
00:24:17,540 --> 00:24:19,800
Next time: "A Gift from Space"

381
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:20,920
Don't send it!

382
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:55,680
Surprise and commotion, at the right moment, solved quickly,
settled and decided, sparks and bouncing, gathered and acted, flying away.

383
00:24:56,660 --> 00:24:59,980
More than anything, incredible power.

384
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:06,380
Gather everyone, if you come here.

385
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:12,640
Like a dream, the final energy.

386
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:17,100
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday.

387
00:25:17,100 --> 00:25:19,980
Drawing the universe, standing on the earth.

388
00:25:19,980 --> 00:25:23,720
The star of Kameari is coming, you see.

389
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:27,460
This should be fine, right?

390
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:29,000
Like hell it's fine!

391
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

